§ `Part 25 Company charges -- Chapter 2 Companies registered in Scotland -- ss 878 to 892`

§§ `s 879 Charges which have to be registered: supplementary (definitions that govern this Chapter)`

-- src:12051 | (6) In this Chapter “company” means an incorporated company registered in Scotland.
@ref s 879(6) In this Chapter "company" means an incorporated company registered in Scotland (src:12051-12051)
GIVEN `the body is an incorporated company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the place where the body is registered` IS A `Place of registration`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 879(6) the body is a company` MEANS
    IF `the body is an incorporated company` AND `the place where the body is registered` EQUALS `Scotland`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In this Chapter “company” means an incorporated company registered in Scotland"

§§ `s 878 Charges created by a company`

DECLARE `s 878(7) what the charge is` HAS
    `a charge on land or any interest in such land` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a charge for any rent or other periodical sum payable in respect of the land` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a security over goodwill` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a security over a patent or a licence under a patent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a security over a trademark` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a security over a copyright or a licence under a copyright` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a security over a registered design or a licence in respect of such a design` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a security over a design right or a licence under a design right` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a security over the book debts (whether book debts of the company or assigned to it)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a security over uncalled share capital of the company or calls made but not paid` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a security over a ship or aircraft or any share in a ship` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a floating charge` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:12030 | (7) This section applies to the following charges—
-- src:12031 | (a) a charge on land or any interest in such land, other than a charge for any rent or other periodical sum payable in respect of the land,
-- src:12032 | (b) a security over incorporeal moveable property of any of the following categories—
-- src:12033 | (i) goodwill,
-- src:12034 | (ii) a patent or a licence under a patent,
-- src:12035 | (iii) a trademark,
-- src:12036 | (iv) a copyright or a licence under a copyright,
-- src:12037 | (v) a registered design or a licence in respect of such a design,
-- src:12038 | (vi) a design right or a licence under a design right,
-- src:12039 | (vii) the book debts (whether book debts of the company or assigned to it), and
-- src:12040 | (viii) uncalled share capital of the company or calls made but not paid,
-- src:12041 | (c) a security over a ship or aircraft or any share in a ship,
-- src:12042 | (d) a floating charge.
@ref s 878(7) This section applies to the following charges (src:12030-12042)
GIVEN charge IS A `s 878(7) what the charge is`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 878(7) the charge is one to which section 878 applies` MEANS
    IF       (charge's `a charge on land or any interest in such land` AND (NOT charge's `a charge for any rent or other periodical sum payable in respect of the land`))
         OR  charge's `a security over goodwill`
         OR  charge's `a security over a patent or a licence under a patent`
         OR  charge's `a security over a trademark`
         OR  charge's `a security over a copyright or a licence under a copyright`
         OR  charge's `a security over a registered design or a licence in respect of such a design`
         OR  charge's `a security over a design right or a licence under a design right`
         OR  charge's `a security over the book debts (whether book debts of the company or assigned to it)`
         OR  charge's `a security over uncalled share capital of the company or calls made but not paid`
         OR  charge's `a security over a ship or aircraft or any share in a ship`
         OR  charge's `a floating charge`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section applies to the following charges—": a scope list with no "only" (fork F-C2 in NOTES.md)

-- src:12020 | (1) A company that creates a charge to which this section applies must deliver the prescribed particulars of the charge, together with a copy certified as a correct copy of the instrument (if any) by which the charge is created or evidenced, to the registrar for registration before the end of the period allowed for registration.
@ref s 878(1) A company that creates a charge to which this section applies must deliver the prescribed particulars of the charge, together with a copy certified as a correct copy of the instrument, to the registrar for registration before the end of the period allowed for registration (src:12020-12020)
GIVEN `the place where the company is registered` IS A `Place of registration`
      `the body is an incorporated company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company creates a charge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 878(7) the charge is one to which section 878 applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 878(1) the company must deliver the prescribed particulars and a certified copy of the instrument to the registrar` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`s 879(6) the body is a company` `the body is an incorporated company` `the place where the company is registered`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In this Chapter “company” means an incorporated company registered in Scotland"
        IF (NOT `the company creates a charge`)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company that creates a charge to which this section applies must deliver"
        IF `s 878(7) the charge is one to which section 878 applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a charge to which this section applies": whether the charge is one the section applies to is not decided by the list in subsection (7)

-- src:12021 | (2) Registration of a charge to which this section applies may instead be effected on the application of a person interested in it.
@ref s 878(2) Registration of a charge to which this section applies may instead be effected on the application of a person interested in it (src:12021-12021)
GIVEN `the person is a person interested in the charge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 878(2) registration may be effected on the application of the person` MEANS
    IF `the person is a person interested in the charge`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on the application of a person interested in it"

-- src:12022 | (3) Where registration is effected on the application of some person other than the company, that person is entitled to recover from the company the amount of any fees properly paid by him to the registrar on the registration.
