GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 878(4) the company fails to comply with subsection (1), so that an offence is committed` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 878(6) subsection (4) applies` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (4) does not apply if registration of the charge has been effected on the application of some other person"
        IF `s 878(1) the company must deliver the prescribed particulars and a certified copy of the instrument to the registrar` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company fails to comply with subsection (1)": there is no duty under subsection (1)
        IF `s 878(1) the company must deliver the prescribed particulars and a certified copy of the instrument to the registrar` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent)
        IF `s 859H(1)(b) the particulars and certified copy were delivered before the end of the period allowed for registration` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 859H(1)(b) the particulars and certified copy were delivered before the end of the period allowed for registration` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company fails to comply with subsection (1)": the company complied
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the period has not yet run out

-- src:12024 | (a) the company, and
@ref s 878(4)(a) the company (src:12024-12024)
