GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 881(3)(a) references in Chapter 2 to a charge are references to the further charge` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 881(2) a further charge is held to have been created`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In that case, the provisions of this Chapter apply to the further charge as if"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent)

-- src:12064 | (3) In that case, the provisions of this Chapter apply to the further charge as if—
@ref s 881(3)(b) references to the date of the creation of a charge were references to the date on which the further back letter or agreement was executed (src:12064-12064)
GIVEN `s 881(2) a further charge is held to have been created` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the further back letter or agreement was executed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 881(3)(b) the date of the creation of the further charge` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 881(2) a further charge is held to have been created`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST `the day on which the further back letter or agreement was executed`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): there is no further charge
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent)

§§ `s 882 Charge in series of debentures`

-- src:12070 | (2) The following are the required particulars—
-- src:12071 | (a) the total amount secured by the whole series,
-- src:12072 | (b) the dates of the resolutions authorising the issue of the series and the date of the covering deed (if any) by which the security is created or defined,
-- src:12073 | (c) a general description of the property charged,
-- src:12074 | (d) the names of the trustees (if any) for the debenture-holders, and
-- src:12075 | (e) in the case of a floating charge, a statement of any provisions of the charge and of any instrument relating to it which prohibit or restrict or regulate the power of the company to grant further securities ranking in priority to, or pari passu with, the floating charge, or which vary or otherwise regulate the order of ranking of the floating charge in relation to subsisting securities.
@ref s 882(2) The following are the required particulars (src:12070-12075)
GIVEN `the particulars give the total amount secured by the whole series` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the particulars give the dates of the resolutions authorising the issue of the series` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is a covering deed by which the security is created or defined` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the particulars give the date of the covering deed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the particulars give a general description of the property charged` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there are trustees for the debenture-holders` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the particulars give the names of the trustees for the debenture-holders` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the charge is a floating charge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the particulars give a statement of any provisions of the charge and of any instrument relating to it which prohibit or restrict or regulate the power of the company to grant further securities ranking in priority to, or pari passu with, the floating charge, or which vary or otherwise regulate the order of ranking of the floating charge in relation to subsisting securities` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 882(2) the particulars given are the required particulars` MEANS
    IF       `the particulars give the total amount secured by the whole series`
         AND `the particulars give the dates of the resolutions authorising the issue of the series`
         AND ((NOT `there is a covering deed by which the security is created or defined`) OR `the particulars give the date of the covering deed`)
         AND `the particulars give a general description of the property charged`
         AND ((NOT `there are trustees for the debenture-holders`) OR `the particulars give the names of the trustees for the debenture-holders`)
         AND ((NOT `the charge is a floating charge`) OR `the particulars give a statement of any provisions of the charge and of any instrument relating to it which prohibit or restrict or regulate the power of the company to grant further securities ranking in priority to, or pari passu with, the floating charge, or which vary or otherwise regulate the order of ranking of the floating charge in relation to subsisting securities`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The following are the required particulars—"

-- src:12069 | (1) Where a series of debentures containing, or giving by reference to any other instrument, any charge to the benefit of which the debenture-holders of that series are entitled pari passu, is created by a company, it is sufficient for purposes of section 878 if the required particulars, together with a copy of the deed containing the charge (or, if there is no such deed, of one of the debentures of the series) are delivered to the registrar before the end of the period allowed for registration.
@ref s 882(1) it is sufficient for purposes of section 878 if the required particulars, together with a copy of the deed containing the charge (or, if there is no such deed, of one of the debentures of the series), are delivered to the registrar before the end of the period allowed for registration (src:12069-12069)
GIVEN `s 738 the instrument is a debenture` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `a series of debentures containing, or giving by reference to any other instrument, a charge to the benefit of which the debenture-holders of that series are entitled pari passu is created by a company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 882(2) the particulars given are the required particulars` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 859H(1)(b) a copy of the deed or of one of the debentures was delivered with the particulars before the end of the period allowed for registration` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 882(1) delivery of the particulars with a copy of the deed or of one debenture is sufficient for section 878` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `a series of debentures containing, or giving by reference to any other instrument, a charge to the benefit of which the debenture-holders of that series are entitled pari passu is created by a company`)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a series of debentures containing, or giving by reference to any other instrument, any charge to the benefit of which the debenture-holders of that series are entitled pari passu, is created by a company"
        IF `s 738 the instrument is a debenture` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a series of debentures"
        IF `s 738 the instrument is a debenture` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the instruments are "debentures" is s 738
        IF (`s 882(2) the particulars given are the required particulars` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`s 859H(1)(b) a copy of the deed or of one of the debentures was delivered with the particulars before the end of the period allowed for registration` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "it is sufficient for purposes of section 878 if": "sufficient if" states a sufficient condition, not a necessary one

-- src:12076 | (3) Where more than one issue is made of debentures in the series, particulars of the date and amount of each issue of debentures of the series must be sent to the registrar for entry in the register of charges.
@ref s 882(3) Where more than one issue is made of debentures in the series, particulars of the date and amount of each issue must be sent to the registrar for entry in the register of charges (src:12076-12076)
GIVEN `more than one issue is made of debentures in the series` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 882(3) particulars of the date and amount of each issue must be sent to the registrar` MEANS
    IF `more than one issue is made of debentures in the series`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where more than one issue is made of debentures in the series"

-- src:12077 | (4) Failure to comply with subsection (3) does not affect the validity of any of those debentures.
@ref s 882(4) Failure to comply with subsection (3) does not affect the validity of any of those debentures (src:12077-12077)
GIVEN `there has been a failure to comply with subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 882(4) the failure to comply with subsection (3) affects the validity of the debentures` MEANS
    IF `there has been a failure to comply with subsection (3)`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Failure to comply with subsection (3) does not affect the validity of any of those debentures"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): there is no failure for subsection (4) to speak of

-- src:12078 | (5) Subsections (2) to (6) of section 878 apply for the purposes of this section as they apply for the purposes of that section but as if for the reference to the registration of the charge there was substituted a reference to the registration of the series of debentures.
@ref s 882(5) Subsections (2) to (6) of section 878 apply for the purposes of this section as they apply for the purposes of that section (src:12078-12078)
GIVEN `the debentures are of a series of the kind mentioned in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 882(5) subsections (2) to (6) of section 878 apply to the registration of the series of debentures` MEANS
    IF `the debentures are of a series of the kind mentioned in subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for the purposes of this section"

§§ `s 883 Additional registration requirement for commission etc in relation to debentures`

-- src:12080 | (1) Where any commission, allowance or discount has been paid or made either directly or indirectly by a company to a person in consideration of his—
-- src:12081 | (a) subscribing or agreeing to subscribe, whether absolutely or conditionally, for debentures in a company, or
-- src:12082 | (b) procuring or agreeing to procure subscriptions, whether absolute or conditional, for such debentures,
-- src:12083 | the particulars required to be sent for registration under section 878 shall include particulars as to the amount or rate per cent. of the commission, discount or allowance so paid or made.
@ref s 883(1) the particulars required to be sent for registration under section 878 shall include particulars as to the amount or rate per cent. of the commission, discount or allowance (src:12080-12083)
GIVEN `s 738 the instrument is a debenture` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `a commission, allowance or discount has been paid or made, directly or indirectly, by a company to a person in consideration of his subscribing or agreeing to subscribe for debentures in a company, or procuring or agreeing to procure subscriptions for them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 883(1) the particulars must include the amount or rate per cent. of the commission, discount or allowance` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `a commission, allowance or discount has been paid or made, directly or indirectly, by a company to a person in consideration of his subscribing or agreeing to subscribe for debentures in a company, or procuring or agreeing to procure subscriptions for them`)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where any commission, allowance or discount has been paid or made either directly or indirectly by a company to a person"
        IF `s 738 the instrument is a debenture` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 738 the instrument is a debenture` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for debentures in a company"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the instruments are "debentures" is s 738

-- src:12084 | (2) The deposit of debentures as security for a debt of the company is not, for the purposes of this section, treated as the issue of debentures at a discount.
@ref s 883(2) The deposit of debentures as security for a debt of the company is not, for the purposes of this section, treated as the issue of debentures at a discount (src:12084-12084)
GIVEN `the debentures are deposited as security for a debt of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 883(2) the deposit is treated as the issue of debentures at a discount` MEANS
    IF `the debentures are deposited as security for a debt of the company`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is not, for the purposes of this section, treated as the issue of debentures at a discount"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (2) says only what the deposit of debentures as security is not

-- src:12085 | (3) Failure to comply with this section does not affect the validity of the debentures issued.
@ref s 883(3) Failure to comply with this section does not affect the validity of the debentures issued (src:12085-12085)
GIVEN `there has been a failure to comply with section 883` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 883(3) the failure to comply with section 883 affects the validity of the debentures issued` MEANS
    IF `there has been a failure to comply with section 883`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Failure to comply with this section does not affect the validity of the debentures issued"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): there is no failure for subsection (3) to speak of

§§ `s 884 Charges on property outside United Kingdom`

-- src:12088 | Where a charge is created in the United Kingdom but comprises property outside the United Kingdom, the copy of the instrument creating or purporting to create the charge may be sent for registration under section 878 even if further proceedings may be necessary to make the charge valid or effectual according to the law of the country in which the property is situated.
@ref s 884 Where a charge is created in the United Kingdom but comprises property outside the United Kingdom, the copy of the instrument may be sent for registration under section 878 even if further proceedings may be necessary (src:12088-12088)
GIVEN `the charge is created in the United Kingdom but comprises property outside the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 884 the copy of the instrument may be sent for registration under section 878 even if further proceedings are necessary` MEANS
    IF `the charge is created in the United Kingdom but comprises property outside the United Kingdom`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a charge is created in the United Kingdom but comprises property outside the United Kingdom"

§§ `s 885 Register of charges to be kept by registrar`

-- src:12091 | (1) The registrar shall keep, with respect to each company, a register of all the charges requiring registration under this Chapter.
@ref s 885(1) The registrar shall keep, with respect to each company, a register of all the charges requiring registration under this Chapter (src:12091-12091)
GIVEN `the charge requires registration under Chapter 2` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 885(1) the registrar must keep the charge in the register of charges` MEANS
    IF `the charge requires registration under Chapter 2`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a register of all the charges requiring registration under this Chapter"

-- src:12092 | (2) In the case of a charge to the benefit of which holders of a series of debentures are entitled, the registrar shall enter in the register the required particulars specified in section 882(2).
@ref s 885(2) In the case of a charge to the benefit of which holders of a series of debentures are entitled, the registrar shall enter in the register the required particulars specified in section 882(2) (src:12092-12092)
GIVEN `the charge is one to the benefit of which holders of a series of debentures are entitled` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 885(2) the registrar must enter the required particulars specified in section 882(2)` MEANS
    IF `the charge is one to the benefit of which holders of a series of debentures are entitled`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In the case of a charge to the benefit of which holders of a series of debentures are entitled"

DECLARE `s 885(3) particular` IS ONE OF
    `s 885(3)(a) the date of its creation`
    `s 885(3)(a) the date of the acquisition`
    `s 885(3)(b) the amount secured by the charge`
    `s 885(3)(c) short particulars of the property charged`
    `s 885(3)(d) the persons entitled to the charge`
    `s 885(3)(e) in the case of a floating charge, a statement of the provisions of the charge and of any instrument relating to it which prohibit or restrict or regulate the company's power to grant further securities ranking in priority to, or pari passu with, the floating charge, or which vary or otherwise regulate the order of ranking of the floating charge in relation to subsisting securities`
    `s 885(3) any other particular`

-- src:12093 | (3) In the case of any other charge, the registrar shall enter in the register the following particulars—
-- src:12094 | (a) if it is a charge created by a company, the date of its creation and, if it is a charge which was existing on property acquired by the company, the date of the acquisition,
-- src:12095 | (b) the amount secured by the charge,
-- src:12096 | (c) short particulars of the property charged,
-- src:12097 | (d) the persons entitled to the charge, and
-- src:12098 | (e) in the case of a floating charge, a statement of any of the provisions of the charge and of any instrument relating to it which prohibit or restrict or regulate the company's power to grant further securities ranking in priority to, or pari passu with, the floating charge, or which vary or otherwise regulate the order of ranking of the floating charge in relation to subsisting securities.
@ref s 885(3) In the case of any other charge, the registrar shall enter in the register the following particulars (src:12093-12098)
GIVEN `the charge is one other than a charge of a series of debentures` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the charge is a charge created by a company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the charge is one which was existing on property acquired by the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the charge is a floating charge` IS A BOOLEAN
      particular IS A `s 885(3) particular`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 885(3) the registrar must enter the particular in the register` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the charge is one other than a charge of a series of debentures`)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In the case of any other charge, the registrar shall enter in the register the following particulars—"
        IF particular EQUALS `s 885(3) any other particular` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "the following particulars—"
        IF particular EQUALS `s 885(3)(a) the date of its creation` THEN (IF `the charge is a charge created by a company` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE)
        IF particular EQUALS `s 885(3)(a) the date of the acquisition` THEN (IF `the charge is one which was existing on property acquired by the company` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE)
        IF particular EQUALS `s 885(3)(e) in the case of a floating charge, a statement of the provisions of the charge and of any instrument relating to it which prohibit or restrict or regulate the company's power to grant further securities ranking in priority to, or pari passu with, the floating charge, or which vary or otherwise regulate the order of ranking of the floating charge in relation to subsisting securities`
        THEN (IF `the charge is a floating charge` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE) -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the case of a floating charge"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `s 885(4) what the certificate states` IS ONE OF
    `s 885(4)(a) the name of the company`
    `s 885(4)(a) the person first-named in the charge among those entitled to the benefit of the charge`
    `s 885(4)(a) in the case of a series of debentures, the name of the holder of the first such debenture issued`
    `s 885(4)(b) the amount secured by the charge`
    `s 885(4) anything else`

-- src:12099 | (4) The registrar shall give a certificate of the registration of any charge registered in pursuance of this Chapter, stating—
-- src:12100 | (a) the name of the company and the person first-named in the charge among those entitled to the benefit of the charge (or, in the case of a series of debentures, the name of the holder of the first such debenture issued), and
-- src:12101 | (b) the amount secured by the charge.
@ref s 885(4) The registrar shall give a certificate of the registration of any charge registered in pursuance of this Chapter, stating (src:12099-12101)
GIVEN `the charge is registered in pursuance of Chapter 2` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the charge is a series of debentures` IS A BOOLEAN
      item IS A `s 885(4) what the certificate states`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 885(4) the certificate of the registration of the charge must state the item` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the charge is registered in pursuance of Chapter 2`)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any charge registered in pursuance of this Chapter": the certificate is that of a charge registered in pursuance of this Chapter; the text says nothing of any other charge
        IF item EQUALS `s 885(4) anything else` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "stating—"
        IF item EQUALS `s 885(4)(a) the person first-named in the charge among those entitled to the benefit of the charge` THEN (IF `the charge is a series of debentures` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST TRUE) -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(or, in the case of a series of debentures, the name of the holder of the first such debenture issued)": for a series the holder of the first debenture is named instead
        IF item EQUALS `s 885(4)(a) in the case of a series of debentures, the name of the holder of the first such debenture issued` THEN (IF `the charge is a series of debentures` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE) -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the case of a series of debentures, the name of the holder of the first such debenture issued"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:12102 | (5) The certificate—
-- src:12103 | (a) shall be signed by the registrar or authenticated by the registrar's official seal, and
-- src:12104 | (b) is conclusive evidence that the requirements of this Chapter as to registration have been satisfied.
@ref s 885(5)(a) The certificate shall be signed by the registrar or authenticated by the registrar's official seal (src:12102-12104)
GIVEN `the certificate is signed by the registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1062 the document bears the registrar's official seal` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 885(5)(a) the certificate is signed or authenticated as the paragraph requires` MEANS
    IF `the certificate is signed by the registrar`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 1062 the document bears the registrar's official seal`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be signed by the registrar or authenticated by the registrar's official seal"
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the certificate bears the official seal is s 1062, which another part answers

-- src:12104 | (b) is conclusive evidence that the requirements of this Chapter as to registration have been satisfied.
@ref s 885(5)(b) The certificate is conclusive evidence that the requirements of this Chapter as to registration have been satisfied (src:12104-12104)
GIVEN `a certificate of the registration of the charge has been given under subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 885(5)(b) the certificate is conclusive evidence that the requirements of Chapter 2 as to registration have been satisfied` MEANS
    IF `a certificate of the registration of the charge has been given under subsection (4)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no certificate has been given

-- src:12105 | (6) The register kept in pursuance of this section shall be open to inspection by any person.
@ref s 885(6) The register kept in pursuance of this section shall be open to inspection by any person (src:12105-12105)
GIVEN `the register is the register kept by the registrar in pursuance of section 885` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 885(6) the register is open to inspection by any person` MEANS
    IF `the register is the register kept by the registrar in pursuance of section 885`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The register kept in pursuance of this section"

§§ `s 886 The period allowed for registration`

-- src:12107 | (1) The period allowed for registration of a charge created by a company is—
-- src:12108 | (a) 21 days beginning with the day after the day on which the charge is created, or
-- src:12109 | (b) if the charge is created outside the United Kingdom, 21 days beginning with the day after the day on which a copy of the instrument by which the charge is created or evidenced could, in due course of post (and if despatched with due diligence) have been received in the United Kingdom.
@ref s 886(1) The period allowed for registration of a charge created by a company (src:12107-12109)
GIVEN `the charge is created outside the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the charge is created` IS A DATE
      `the day on which a copy of the instrument by which the charge is created or evidenced could, in due course of post (and if despatched with due diligence) have been received in the United Kingdom` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 886(1) the last day of the period allowed for registration of a charge created by a company` MEANS
    IF `the charge is created outside the United Kingdom`
    THEN `s 859A(4) the last day of 21 days beginning with the day after` `the day on which a copy of the instrument by which the charge is created or evidenced could, in due course of post (and if despatched with due diligence) have been received in the United Kingdom`
    ELSE `s 859A(4) the last day of 21 days beginning with the day after` `the day on which the charge is created`

-- src:12110 | (2) The period allowed for registration of a charge to which property acquired by a company is subject is—
-- src:12111 | (a) 21 days beginning with the day after the day on which the transaction is settled, or
-- src:12112 | (b) if the property is situated and the charge was created outside the United Kingdom, 21 days beginning with the day after the day on which a copy of the instrument by which the charge is created or evidenced could, in due course of post (and if despatched with due diligence) have been received in the United Kingdom.
@ref s 886(2) The period allowed for registration of a charge to which property acquired by a company is subject (src:12110-12112)
GIVEN `the property is situated and the charge was created outside the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the transaction is settled` IS A DATE
      `the day on which a copy of the instrument by which the charge is created or evidenced could, in due course of post (and if despatched with due diligence) have been received in the United Kingdom` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 886(2) the last day of the period allowed for registration of a charge to which property acquired by a company is subject` MEANS
    IF `the property is situated and the charge was created outside the United Kingdom`
    THEN `s 859A(4) the last day of 21 days beginning with the day after` `the day on which a copy of the instrument by which the charge is created or evidenced could, in due course of post (and if despatched with due diligence) have been received in the United Kingdom`
    ELSE `s 859A(4) the last day of 21 days beginning with the day after` `the day on which the transaction is settled`

-- src:12113 | (3) The period allowed for registration of particulars of a series of debentures as a result of section 882 is—
-- src:12114 | (a) if there is a deed containing the charge mentioned in section 882(1), 21 days beginning with the day after the day on which that deed is executed, or
-- src:12115 | (b) if there is no such deed, 21 days beginning with the day after the day on which the first debenture of the series is executed.
@ref s 886(3) The period allowed for registration of particulars of a series of debentures as a result of section 882 (src:12113-12115)
GIVEN `there is a deed containing the charge mentioned in section 882(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which that deed is executed` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the first debenture of the series is executed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 886(3) the last day of the period allowed for registration of particulars of a series of debentures` MEANS
    IF `there is a deed containing the charge mentioned in section 882(1)`
    THEN `s 859A(4) the last day of 21 days beginning with the day after` `the day on which that deed is executed`
    ELSE `s 859A(4) the last day of 21 days beginning with the day after` `the day on which the first debenture of the series is executed`

§§ `s 887 Entries of satisfaction and relief`

-- src:12117 | (1) Subsection (2) applies if a statement is delivered to the registrar verifying with respect to any registered charge—
-- src:12118 | (a) that the debt for which the charge was given has been paid or satisfied in whole or in part, or
-- src:12119 | (b) that part of the property charged has been released from the charge or has ceased to form part of the company's property.
@ref s 887(1) Subsection (2) applies if a statement is delivered to the registrar verifying with respect to any registered charge that the debt has been paid or satisfied, or that part of the property has been released (src:12117-12119)
GIVEN `a statement is delivered to the registrar verifying that the debt for which the charge was given has been paid or satisfied in whole or in part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a statement is delivered to the registrar verifying that part of the property charged has been released from the charge or has ceased to form part of the company's property` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 887(1) subsection (2) applies` MEANS
    IF `a statement is delivered to the registrar verifying that the debt for which the charge was given has been paid or satisfied in whole or in part` OR `a statement is delivered to the registrar verifying that part of the property charged has been released from the charge or has ceased to form part of the company's property`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (2) applies if a statement is delivered to the registrar verifying with respect to any registered charge—"

-- src:12120 | (2) If the charge is a floating charge, the statement must be accompanied by either—
-- src:12121 | (a) a statement by the creditor entitled to the benefit of the charge, or a person authorised by him for the purpose, verifying that the statement mentioned in subsection (1) is correct, or
-- src:12122 | (b) a direction obtained from the court, on the ground that the statement by the creditor mentioned in paragraph (a) could not be readily obtained, dispensing with the need for that statement.
@ref s 887(2) If the charge is a floating charge, the statement must be accompanied by either a statement by the creditor verifying that the statement is correct, or a direction obtained from the court dispensing with the need for that statement (src:12120-12122)
GIVEN `s 887(1) subsection (2) applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the charge is a floating charge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement is accompanied by a statement by the creditor entitled to the benefit of the charge, or a person authorised by him for the purpose, verifying that the statement mentioned in subsection (1) is correct` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement is accompanied by a direction obtained from the court, on the ground that the statement by the creditor could not be readily obtained, dispensing with the need for that statement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 887(2) the statement is accompanied as the subsection requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 887(1) subsection (2) applies` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (2) applies if"
        IF (NOT `the charge is a floating charge`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the charge is a floating charge": a charge that is not a floating charge is not one for which the subsection requires accompaniment (marginal reading (a); the other readings, TRUE as nothing is required and NOTHING as the text is silent, are in fork F-M1 in NOTES.md)
        IF `s 887(1) subsection (2) applies` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent)
        IF `the statement is accompanied by a statement by the creditor entitled to the benefit of the charge, or a person authorised by him for the purpose, verifying that the statement mentioned in subsection (1) is correct` OR `the statement is accompanied by a direction obtained from the court, on the ground that the statement by the creditor could not be readily obtained, dispensing with the need for that statement`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the statement must be accompanied by either—": a bare "must", not met (fork F-P1 in NOTES.md)

-- src:12123 | (3) The registrar may enter on the register a memorandum of satisfaction (in whole or in part) regarding the fact contained in the statement mentioned in subsection (1).
@ref s 887(3) The registrar may enter on the register a memorandum of satisfaction (in whole or in part) regarding the fact contained in the statement (src:12123-12123)
GIVEN `s 887(1) subsection (2) applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 887(3) the registrar may enter a memorandum of satisfaction on the register` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 887(1) subsection (2) applies`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subsection (2) applies if": the power is given on that gate and the text does not say it has none otherwise
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent)

-- src:12124 | (4) Where the registrar enters a memorandum of satisfaction in whole, he shall, if required, furnish the company with a copy of the memorandum.
@ref s 887(4) Where the registrar enters a memorandum of satisfaction in whole, he shall, if required, furnish the company with a copy of the memorandum (src:12124-12124)
GIVEN `the registrar enters a memorandum of satisfaction in whole` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company requires a copy` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 887(4) the registrar must furnish the company with a copy of the memorandum` MEANS
    IF `the registrar enters a memorandum of satisfaction in whole` AND `the company requires a copy`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the registrar enters a memorandum of satisfaction in whole, he shall, if required, furnish the company with a copy of the memorandum"

-- src:12125 | (5) Nothing in this section requires the company to submit particulars with respect to the entry in the register of a memorandum of satisfaction where the company, having created a floating charge over all or any part of its property, disposes of part of the property subject to the floating charge.
@ref s 887(5) Nothing in this section requires the company to submit particulars with respect to the entry in the register of a memorandum of satisfaction where the company, having created a floating charge, disposes of part of the property subject to it (src:12125-12125)
GIVEN `the company, having created a floating charge over all or any part of its property, disposes of part of the property subject to the floating charge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 887(5) this section requires the company to submit particulars with respect to the entry of a memorandum of satisfaction` MEANS
    IF `the company, having created a floating charge over all or any part of its property, disposes of part of the property subject to the floating charge`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this section requires the company to submit particulars with respect to the entry in the register of a memorandum of satisfaction"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (5) says only what the section does not require in that case

§§ `s 888 Rectification of register of charges`

-- src:12127 | (1) Subsection (2) applies if the court is satisfied—
-- src:12128 | (a) that the failure to register a charge before the end of the period allowed for registration, or the omission or mis-statement of any particular with respect to any such charge or in a memorandum of satisfaction—
-- src:12129 | (i) was accidental or due to inadvertence or to some other sufficient cause, or
-- src:12130 | (ii) is not of a nature to prejudice the position of creditors or shareholders of the company, or
-- src:12131 | (b) that on other grounds it is just and equitable to grant relief.
@ref s 888(1) Subsection (2) applies if the court is satisfied (src:12127-12131)
GIVEN `the court is satisfied that the failure to register a charge before the end of the period allowed for registration, or the omission or mis-statement of a particular, was accidental or due to inadvertence or to some other sufficient cause` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that the failure, omission or mis-statement is not of a nature to prejudice the position of creditors or shareholders of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that on other grounds it is just and equitable to grant relief` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 888(1) subsection (2) applies` MEANS
    IF       `the court is satisfied that the failure to register a charge before the end of the period allowed for registration, or the omission or mis-statement of a particular, was accidental or due to inadvertence or to some other sufficient cause`
         OR  `the court is satisfied that the failure, omission or mis-statement is not of a nature to prejudice the position of creditors or shareholders of the company`
         OR  `the court is satisfied that on other grounds it is just and equitable to grant relief`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (2) applies if the court is satisfied—"

DECLARE `s 888(2) order` IS ONE OF
    `s 888(2) an order that the period allowed for registration shall be extended`
    `s 888(2) an order that the omission or mis-statement shall be rectified`
    `s 888(2) any other order`

-- src:12132 | (2) The court may, on the application of the company or a person interested, and on such terms and conditions as seem to the court just and expedient, order that the period allowed for registration shall be extended or, as the case may be, that the omission or mis-statement shall be rectified.
@ref s 888(2) The court may, on the application of the company or a person interested, order that the period allowed for registration shall be extended or that the omission or mis-statement shall be rectified (src:12132-12132)
GIVEN `s 888(1) subsection (2) applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the application is made by the company or a person interested` IS A BOOLEAN
      order IS A `s 888(2) order`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 888(2) the court may make the order` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 888(1) subsection (2) applies`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subsection (2) applies if the court is satisfied—": the power is given on that gate and the text does not say it has none otherwise
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent)
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        BRANCH
            IF (NOT `the application is made by the company or a person interested`)
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on the application of the company or a person interested"
            IF order EQUALS `s 888(2) any other order`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "order that the period allowed for registration shall be extended or, as the case may be, that the omission or mis-statement shall be rectified"
            OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:12132 | (2) The court may, on the application of the company or a person interested, and on such terms and conditions as seem to the court just and expedient, order that the period allowed for registration shall be extended or, as the case may be, that the omission or mis-statement shall be rectified.
@ref s 888(2) the period allowed for registration shall be extended (src:12132-12132)
GIVEN `the last day of the period allowed for registration` IS A DATE
      `the last day to which an order under subsection (2) extends the period` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 888(2) the last day of the period allowed for registration as extended` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the last day to which an order under subsection (2) extends the period`
    WHEN JUST lastDay THEN lastDay
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the last day of the period allowed for registration`

§§ `s 889 Charges void unless registered`

DECLARE `s 889(1) party against whom the charge may be void` IS ONE OF
    `s 889(1)(a) the liquidator of the company`
    `s 889(1)(b) an administrator of the company`
    `s 889(1)(c) any creditor of the company`
    `s 889(1) any other person`

-- src:12135 | (1) If a company creates a charge to which section 878 applies, the charge is void (so far as any security on the company's property or any part of it is conferred by the charge) against—
-- src:12136 | (a) the liquidator of the company,
-- src:12137 | (b) an administrator of the company, and
-- src:12138 | (c) any creditor of the company
-- src:12139 | unless that section is complied with.
@ref s 889(1) If a company creates a charge to which section 878 applies, the charge is void (so far as any security on the company's property or any part of it is conferred by the charge) against the liquidator, an administrator and any creditor unless that section is complied with (src:12135-12139)
GIVEN `a company creates a charge to which section 878 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `section 878 is complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
      party IS A `s 889(1) party against whom the charge may be void`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 889(1) the charge is void against the party` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `a company creates a charge to which section 878 applies`)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company creates a charge to which section 878 applies"
        IF `section 878 is complied with`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless that section is complied with"
        IF party EQUALS `s 889(1) any other person`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "the charge is void (so far as any security on the company's property or any part of it is conferred by the charge) against—"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:12140 | (2) Subsection (1) is without prejudice to any contract or obligation for repayment of the money secured by the charge; and when a charge becomes void under this section the money secured by it immediately becomes payable.
@ref s 889(2) Subsection (1) is without prejudice to any contract or obligation for repayment of the money secured by the charge (src:12140-12140)
GIVEN `there is a contract or obligation for repayment of the money secured by the charge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 889(2) subsection (1) prejudices the contract or obligation for repayment of the money secured by the charge` MEANS
    IF `there is a contract or obligation for repayment of the money secured by the charge`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) is without prejudice to any contract or obligation for repayment of the money secured by the charge"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): there is nothing for subsection (1) to prejudice

-- src:12140 | (2) Subsection (1) is without prejudice to any contract or obligation for repayment of the money secured by the charge; and when a charge becomes void under this section the money secured by it immediately becomes payable.
@ref s 889(2) when a charge becomes void under this section the money secured by it immediately becomes payable (src:12140-12140)
GIVEN `s 889(1) the charge is void against the party` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 889(2) the money secured by the charge immediately becomes payable` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 889(1) the charge is void against the party`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "when a charge becomes void under this section the money secured by it immediately becomes payable": "when" counts as "where"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent)

§§ `s 890 Copies of instruments creating charges to be kept by company`

-- src:12143 | (1) Every company shall cause a copy of every instrument creating a charge requiring registration under this Chapter to be kept available for inspection.
