    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If an officer of the company knowingly and wilfully authorises or permits the omission of an entry required to be made in pursuance of this section"
    ELSE `s 1173(1) the holder of the position is an officer of the body corporate`

-- src:12149 | (4) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable—
-- src:12150 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to a fine;
-- src:12151 | (b) on summary conviction, to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum.
@ref s 891(4) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on conviction on indictment to a fine, on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum (src:12149-12151)
`s 891(4) the penalties for the offence` MEANS
    LIST (Penalty OF `on conviction on indictment`, NOTHING, JUST `a fine without a stated limit`, NOTHING, FALSE)
         , (Penalty OF `on summary conviction`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, FALSE)

§§ `s 892 Instruments creating charges and register of charges to be available for inspection`

-- src:12153 | (1) This section applies to—
